=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ HASS @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt vms-hass agent @VERSION@ for OpenVMS: publishes this system to Home Assistant over MQTT
1 'NOTICE
=prompt The vms-hass agent for OpenVMS is distributed under the MIT licence.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [HASS.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for the vms-hass agent
    Once, as SYSTEM: create or check the agent's account (default HASS, with a
    UIC group of its own above MAXSYSGROUP), set the protections, and create
    HASS$ROOT:[CONF]AGENT.CONF from its template:
    $ @HASS$ROOT:[COM]HASS$CONFIGURE
    Put the broker's address and user in HASS$ROOT:[CONF]AGENT.CONF, and the
    user's password in HASS$ROOT:[CONF]MQTT.PWD; run HASS$CONFIGURE again
    to protect both, then:
    $ @HASS$ROOT:[COM]HASS$CONTROL START
    At boot, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (after TCP/IP):
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:HASS$STARTUP.COM
    At shutdown, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSHUTDWN.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:HASS$SHUTDOWN.COM

PRODUCT REMOVE HASS stops the agent and deassigns HASS$ROOT; the
configuration, the password file, the node ID, the logs and the account
are kept, and so is the device in Home Assistant (HASS_AGENT --REMOVE
removes it first, if you want that).
